## Summary

Implemented **`DET.LAYOUT.GRID_CONSISTENCY`** as a Playwright/DOM deterministic check aligned with the catalog rule: content should sit on the layout grid (max width + gutters), without accidental full-bleed prose.

### What changed

1. **`design-rules/deterministic/generated/det-layout-grid-consistency.check.js`**
   - **`full-bleed-prose`** (`warn`): substantive paragraphs (≥32 words) in `main` that are not inside a grid container (`.container`, `.doc-content`, max-width ancestors, etc.) and span ≥88% of the main column or ≥82% of the viewport.
   - **`gutter-drift`** (`minor`): within the same `section`/`article`, prose left edges differ by more than 56px.
   - **`excessive-measure`** (`minor`): prose inside a grid container but wider than 920px.
   - Heroes, tables, code, modals, and explicit bleed regions are excluded.
   - Exports: `rule`, `run`, `collectLayoutGridConsistencyReport`, `findingsFromLayoutGridReport`, and testable helpers.

2. **`design-rules/blender/rule-mappings.js`**
   - Registered under `DETERMINISTIC_IMPLEMENTATIONS` as **`implemented`**: `area: readability`, `scoreDimension: visualRhythmFirstScreen`, `defaultSeverity: warn`, `priorityWeight: 7`.

3. **`auditor-tests/det-layout-grid-consistency.test.js`**
   - Unit tests for helpers, finding mapping, and `run()` with `metrics.layoutGridConsistencyReport`.

4. **`design-rules/registry.generated.json`**
   - Moved `DET.LAYOUT.GRID_CONSISTENCY` from stub → implemented (partial update). **Re-run `npm run blend-rules`** to refresh the full registry fingerprint and any other mapping drift.

### Why these signals

They match the doc anchor without AI: measurable width/inset vs main and viewport, KS container patterns (`.doc-content`, Bootstrap containers), and gutter consistency within sections—same pattern as `det-chrome-boundary.check.js` (collect in browser → map to standard finding fields).

